  "raw": {
    "https://www.westmont.edu/office-provost/open-positions#a6HVW0000002I0r2AE": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Nursing (Med/Surg - 3 positions)",
      "description": "Westmont College seeks qualified and motivated nursing faculty members to serve in its graduate (MEPN/CNL and MSN/CNL) and undergraduate (ABSN) nursing programs. These positions focuse on teaching, mentoring, and contributing to the growth of our nursing program. We are looking for a candidate with a strong clinical and academic background who is passionate about educating and inspiring the next generation of nursing professionals. Candidates should demonstrate a commitment to excellence in nursing education, student formation, scholarly research, and professional practice. Responsibilities: Develop and teach graduate nursing courses Integrate Christian faith with teaching and learning Mentor and advise students in academic, clinical, and professional development Contribute to curriculum development and program implementation Engage in scholarly and professional activity Support clinical partnerships and student learning experiences Participate in faculty governance, program evaluation, and accreditation processes Qualifications: Doctoral degree in nursing (DNP or PhD) required Current RN license (California eligibility required) Expertise in clinical practice, leadership, or systems-based care Teaching or mentoring experience preferred Faculty members are expected to wholeheartedly embrace the mission of the College, in the Protestant evangelical tradition. Westmont is a Christian liberal arts college. We seek faculty from diverse racial and ethnic backgrounds who are committed to graduate and undergraduate teaching, scholarly activity, and the integration of faith. The college seeks to enrich its educational experience and its culture through the diversity of its faculty, administration, staff, and students. Diverse candidates from historically underrepresented groups are especially encouraged to apply Anticipated Hiring Range $121497 - $136685 The pay range posted for this job opening reflects what Westmont College reasonably expects to pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation will vary based on relevant factors such as work experience, education, training, skill level, and market conditions. Apply for this Position"
    },
    "https://www.westmont.edu/office-provost/open-positions#a6HVW00000079hh2AA": {
      "title": "Visiting Instructor or Assistant Professor of Chemistry",
      "description": "Qualifications: A minimum of a Master’s degree in chemistry is required. A doctoral degree is strongly preferred. The candidate should have good teaching and communication abilities. The candidate should be willing and able to create course syllabi, instructional materials, assignments and assessments. Position Summary: The visiting assistant professor position is a full-time position that includes teaching General Chemistry lecture and/or labs, Physical Chemistry 1 & 2 (Quantum Mechanics and Thermodynamics), experimental physical chemistry lab and a general education chemistry course for non-majors (Chemistry, Culture & the Environment). Responsibilities: (teaching duties may vary depending on departmental needs and candidate qualifications) -\tTeaching and preparing two General Chemistry course sections in Fall 2026 -OR- -\tTeaching four General Chemistry Lab sections in Fall 2026 -\tTeaching and preparing one Physical Chemistry 1 (Quantum Mechanics) course in Fall 2026 -\tTeaching and preparing one Physical Chemistry 2 (Thermodynamics) course in Spring 2027 -\tTeaching and preparing one Experimental Physical Chemistry Lab course in Spring 2027 -\tTeaching and preparing one Chemistry, Culture & the Environment (General Education) course in Spring 2027 Reports to: Chemistry Department Chair, Provos Anticipated Hiring Range $70841 - $75219 The pay range posted for this job opening reflects what Westmont College reasonably expects to pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation will vary based on relevant factors such as work experience, education, training, skill level, and market conditions. Apply for this Position"
    },
    "https://www.westmont.edu/office-provost/open-positions#a6HVW0000008SIT2A2": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology - Behavioral Neuroscience",
      "description": "The Psychology department at Westmont College invites applications for a tenure-track position in Psychology that will start in August 2027. Candidates must have a Ph.D. in psychology or neuroscience and evidence of scholarship in behavioral neuroscience. The Psychology department is highly regarded for its ability to prepare students for meaningful careers and successful postgraduate study. We seek applicants with a serious commitment to high-quality undergraduate teaching across various topics in psychology in a Christian liberal arts setting. Candidates must be willing to supervise undergraduate student research and conduct research that collaboratively involves students. It is essential that interested candidates possess the ability to teach, advise, and mentor undergraduate students from diverse and underrepresented backgrounds. Westmont College is a national liberal arts college in the Protestant evangelical tradition. Faculty members are expected to wholeheartedly embrace the mission of the College and to demonstrate excellence in teaching with a commitment to mentoring undergraduate students and having an active scholarly participation. Questions may be addressed to Dr. Andrea Gurney at gurney@westmont.edu . Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Anticipated Hiring Range $74,119 - $77,419 The pay range posted for this job opening reflects what Westmont College reasonably expects to pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation will vary based on relevant factors such as work experience, education, training, skill level, and market conditions. Apply for this Position"
    },
    "https://www.westmont.edu/office-provost/open-positions#a6HVW0000008SK62AM": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Kinesiology - Biomechanics",
      "description": "The Westmont Kinesiology Department invites applications for a tenure-track position. The position has a 3/3 load with the primary teaching focus of a Biomechanics Lecture and Lab, as well as elective classes in the candidate’s specialization and/or classes that meet the needs of the Department. In addition to teaching excellence, candidates are expected to engage in scholarly activity appropriate to their discipline, including the mentorship of undergraduate students in their research endeavors. Promising candidates will have a faithful commitment to the mission of Westmont College, a PhD or an equivalent terminal degree, evidence of effective teaching, and an active research program or the skills and interest to begin one. Westmont College is a national liberal arts college in the Protestant evangelical tradition. Faculty members are expected to wholeheartedly embrace the mission of the College and engage students from all backgrounds with the express intent of whole-person formation and flourishing. Among the benefits of employment are a faculty housing program that makes living in Santa Barbara, California affordable, a generous retirement match, and being an important part of a small community of learners. For questions, please contact Dr. Isaac Gomez, Kinesiology search chair at igomez@westmont.edu . The application will ask for a cover letter, CV, and 3 brief statements (500-1500 words) related to working in the context of the Westmont College community. In the cover letter, applicants should indicate specific ways in which they can actively embrace the identity and mission of the college. Applicants must also indicate agreement with the Articles of Faith and support for the standards and principles enumerated in the Community Life Statement. Anticipated Hiring Range $74,119 - $77,419 The pay range posted for this job opening reflects what Westmont College reasonably expects to pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation will vary based on relevant factors such as work experience, education, training, skill level, and market conditions. Apply for this Position"
    },
    "https://www.westmont.edu/office-provost/open-positions#a6HVW0000008SLh2AM": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Education",
      "description": "The Education Department of Westmont College invites applications for a tenure-track, Assistant Professor of Education position to begin August 2027. The ideal candidate would have substantial elementary education experience and be willing to teach a variety of courses in the Liberal Studies (elementary education) major and teaching credential program. The area of expertise within elementary education is open, but interest in teaching cultural diversity and social studies courses is desireable. Westmont College is a Christian liberal arts college in beautiful Santa Barbara, California with a strong mission rooted in the Protestant evangelical tradition. Benefits include a generous faculty housing program that makes living in Santa Barbara affordable. Responsibilities: Teach 24 units per academic year (typically 3 courses per semester) Engage in scholarly and professional activity Integrate Christian faith with teaching and scholarly activity Mentor and advise students interested in elementary education Contribute to curriculum development and accreditation activities Participate in institutional, professional, and community service Required Qualifications: A relevant doctorate. PhD is preferred, but EdD or ABD will also be considered. At least three years full-time elementary public school teaching experience Demonstrated potential for scholarly activity and college-level teaching Experience supporting students from diverse and underrepresented backgrounds Westmont College is a national liberal arts college in the Protestant evangelical tradition. Faculty members are expected to wholeheartedly embrace the mission of the College and to demonstrate excellence in teaching with a commitment to mentoring undergraduate students and having an active scholarly participation. Questions may be addressed to Dr. Carolyn Mitten ( cmitten@westmont.edu ) . Review of applications will begin November 15th, 2026 and will continue until the position if filled. Anticipated Hiring Range $74,119 - $77,419 The pay range posted for this job opening reflects what Westmont College reasonably expects to pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation will vary based on relevant factors such as work experience, education, training, skill level, and market conditions. Apply for this Position"
    },
    "https://www.westmont.edu/office-provost/open-positions#a6HVW0000008Txh2AE": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of American History",
      "description": "Westmont College invites applications for a tenure-track position in U.S. History at the rank of assistant professor. Ph.D in history required. With a teaching load of three courses per semester, the successful candidate will be expected to teach a combination of lower and upper-division courses in U.S. History including broad survey courses and courses in his or her field of specialization. In addition, several of these courses will need to support the \"Thinking Historically\" and \"Justice, Reconciliation, and Diversity\" aspects of Westmont's General Education program. Westmont College is a national liberal arts college in the Protestant evangelical tradition. Faculty members are expected to wholeheartedly embrace the mission of the College. They must also demonstrate excellence in teaching with a commitment to mentoring undergraduate students, and have an active research agenda. With the changing demographics of our region, over forty percent of our students now identify as non-white, and we are especially interested in faculty who are able to support and encourage students of color and first-generation students. Review of applications will begin November 30th and will continue until the position is filled. Questions may be addressed to the department chair, Dr. Marianne Robins at robins@westmont.edu . Anticipated Hiring Range $74,119 - $77,419 The pay range posted for this job opening reflects what Westmont College reasonably expects to pay for this position at the time of posting. Actual compensation will vary based on relevant factors such as work experience, education, training, skill level, and market conditions. Apply for this Position"
    }
